b61b7a5e.desc:
WHO ARE WE
 Cognism is the leading provider of European B2B data and sales intelligence. Ambitious businesses of every size use our platform to discover, connect, and engage with qualified decision-makers faster and close more deals. Headquartered in London with global offices, Cognism’s contact data and contextual signals are trusted by thousands of revenue teams to eliminate the guesswork from prospecting.
 OUR WORK MODEL   &nbsp; 
 Hybrid: This is a hybrid role, requiring you to work from our Paris office at least 2 days per week, with flexibility to work remotely on other days.  &nbsp; 
 YOUR ROLE   &nbsp; 
 As an Account Manager , you will be responsible for growing and retaining a portfolio of Mid-Market &amp; Enterprise customers by managing renewals and identifying expansion opportunities. You will proactively engage with decision-makers, lead commercial negotiations, and maximize revenue from your accounts. In this high-growth, fast-paced environment, you’ll play a key role in scaling our Account Management function and driving long-term customer success.  &nbsp; 
 YOUR CHALLENGES &amp; OPPORTUNITIES   &nbsp; 
 Drive Revenue Growth – Manage a portfolio of Mid-Market &amp; Enterprise customers, ensuring successful renewals, upsells, and cross-sells.  &nbsp; 
 Expand Customer Relationships – Build strong connections beyond your main point of contact to engage multiple stakeholders, decision-makers, and buying groups within each account.  &nbsp; 
 Strategic Account Management – Work closely with Customer Success Managers to align on customer health and develop tailored renewal and expansion strategies.  &nbsp; 
 Lead Sales Processes – Own the full sales cycle for upsells, from identifying opportunities to conducting demos, negotiating pricing, and closing deals.  &nbsp; 
 Customer Engagement &amp; Advocacy – Leverage customer insights to position Cognism’s product suite effectively, driving adoption and identifying growth potential.  &nbsp; 
 Retention &amp; Risk Mitigation – Monitor customer satisfaction, proactively addressing risks to ensure high retention rates.  &nbsp; 
 Optimize Processes – Contribute to the rollout of new account management workflows, ensuring efficiency and scalability in a rapidly growing team.  &nbsp; 
 OUR EXPECTATIONS   &nbsp; 
 Sales Experience – Proven success in a client-facing role, managing a book of business and exceeding revenue targets.  &nbsp; 
 Commercial Acumen – Confident in running commercial negotiations and guiding customers toward the best Cognism package for their needs.  &nbsp; 
 Proactive &amp; Strategic – Ability to identify expansion opportunities, engage new buying groups, and drive customer growth.  &nbsp; 
 Communication Excellence – Strong ability to build relationships, influence stakeholders, and articulate value propositions clearly.  &nbsp; 
 Process-Driven – Structured approach to pipeline and account management, with attention to detail and responsiveness.  &nbsp; 
 Collaborative Mindset – Team player who thrives in a fast-paced environment and works cross-functionally to achieve shared goals.  &nbsp; 
 Goal-Oriented &amp; Ambitious – Motivated by targets, with a track record of meeting and exceeding sales quotas.  &nbsp; 
 &nbsp;
 WHY COGNISM
 At Cognism, we’re not just building a company - we’re building an inclusive community of brilliant, diverse people who&nbsp; support, challenge, and inspire each other every day . If you’re looking for a place where your work truly&nbsp; makes an impact , you’re in the right spot!
 Our values aren’t just words on a page—they guide how we work, how we treat each other, and how we grow together. They shape our culture, drive our success, and ensure that everyone feels valued, heard, and empowered to do their best work.
 Here’s what we stand for:
 🤝 We Own the Outcome Together. 
🤓&nbsp; We Deeply Understand our Customers.&nbsp; 
🏆&nbsp; We Celebrate Impact Wherever It Comes From. 
 At Cognism, we are committed to fostering an inclusive, diverse, and supportive workplace. We welcome applications from individuals typically underrepresented in tech, so if this role excites you but you’re unsure if you meet every requirement, we encourage you to apply!
 &nbsp;

eada88e3.desc:
&nbsp;
 EBANX is the leading payment platform connecting global companies with customers from the fastest-growing digital markets in the world.
Since the beginning of our journey, we have had one mission: to provide global access for everyone. We believe that transforming challenges into opportunities and making the impossible part of the journey is crucial! That's precisely why we created a payment technology that builds bridges between people and businesses every day in 29 rising markets across the globe.
We call ourselves ebankers, we are global thinkers, we value diversity, we foster creativity and we work hard to connect businesses and people worldwide through payments. Let's make history together?
 We are seeking a Specialist based in Cairo, Egypt , working in a hybrid model , with a focus on growing EBANX’s payments business in Egypt and supporting expansion and sales across other MENA countries as needed. In this role, you will combine market expansion activities with hands-on commercial support, building local partnerships, coordinating integrations, and working alongside Commercial teams to move merchant opportunities through closing, go-live, and ramp-up. Reporting to the MENAT Regional Director, you will collaborate closely with Partnerships, Legal, Product, Pricing, Fin Ops, Technology, and Operations. While the Regional Director leads strategy and negotiations, you will drive execution, research, follow-up, and day-to-day relationships to turn market opportunities into business growth.
 Your day-to-day impact: 
 Build local partnerships: Research and map acquirers, banks, and PSPs in Egypt, coordinate partner evaluations with internal teams, and maintain relationships while supporting negotiations and agreement execution alongside the Regional Director;
 Coordinate partner integrations: Work with Operations, Product, and Technology to track integration milestones, flag blockers early, and improve payment-method coverage, costs, and approval rates through partner performance analysis;
 Support commercial opportunities through closing: Join new sales, account management, and channel meetings to present Egypt and other MENA markets, explain EBANX’s value proposition by market and vertical, and prepare proposals and responses to merchant questions;
 Turn signed deals into merchant growth: Follow opportunities with the Commercial team through closing, go-live, and ramp-up, support activation campaigns, and review checkout and payment flows from a local consumer’s perspective to identify improvements;
 Track performance &amp; maintain visibility: Keep accurate opportunity records and report pipeline progress, TPV, revenue, share of wallet, payment mix, and projections systematically to the Regional Director;
 Support regional expansion &amp; market intelligence: Follow up with Regulatory, Tax, and Finance on Egypt-related matters, support research and partner mapping across other MENA markets, and share reusable learnings. Conduct regular competitor research, represent EBANX at industry events, and contribute to regional studies and thought-leadership content;
 Must-haves to shine in this role: 
 Relevant industry experience: Experience in payments, fintech, banking, or business development;
 Egyptian payments knowledge: Understanding of local payment methods, the payments ecosystem, and the regulatory environment in Egypt;
 Commercial confidence: Comfortable presenting to merchants, explaining market opportunities, and supporting sales conversations through deal closing;
 Analytical &amp; reporting skills: Strong research and analytical capabilities, with confidence using spreadsheets, tracking pipelines, and reporting business performance;
 Negotiation &amp; relationship skills: Ability to build productive relationships with partners, merchants, and internal teams while working alongside senior colleagues;
 Hands-on execution: A proactive, organized approach to managing multiple markets and priorities, following up on deliverables, and escalating blockers early;
 English &amp; Arabic fluency: Fluent written and spoken English and Arabic, with the ability to communicate clearly across commercial and cross-functional discussions;
 Location &amp; travel availability: Based in Cairo, Egypt, available to work in a hybrid model and willing to travel across the region;
 Bonus points if you have: 
 Regional market exposure: Previous experience working in Egypt or other MENA markets;
 Local partner experience: Experience engaging banks, acquirers, or PSPs, including supporting partner evaluations, negotiations, or onboarding;
 Expansion &amp; integration experience: Exposure to market expansion activities or coordinating payment partner integrations;
